1
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:06,000
The world has enough Superheroes.

2
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:06,000
Venom is a science fiction, action film directed by Ruben Fleischer.

3
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:06,000
Investigative journalist Eddie Brock attempts a comeback following a scandal, but
accidentally becomes the host of Venom, a violent, super powerful alien symbiote.

4
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:06,000
Soon, he must rely on his newfound powers to protect the world from a
shadowy organization looking for a symbiote of their own.

5
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:06,000
Eddie Brock / Venom, played by Tom Hardy.

6
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:06,000
Anne Weying, played by Michelle Williams.

7
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:06,000
Carlton Drake / Riot, played by Riz Ahmed.

8
00:32:00,000 --> 00:32:06,000
Security Chief Roland Treece, played by Scott Haze.

9
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:06,000
Dr. Dan Lewis, played by Reid Scott.

10
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:06,000
Dr. Dora Skirth, played by Jenny Slate.

11
00:44:00,000 --> 00:44:06,000
Venom is a 2018 American superhero film based on
the character from Marvel Comics.

12
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
The first film in Sony's Spider-Man Universe (SSU), it was directed by Ruben Fleischer
from a screenplay by Jeff Pinkner, Scott Rosenberg, and Kelly Marcel.

13
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:06,000
Tom Hardy stars as Eddie Brock and Venom, alongside Michelle
Williams, Riz Ahmed, Scott Haze, and Reid Scott.

14
00:56:00,000 --> 00:56:06,000
In the film, Eddie, a struggling journalist, gains superpowers after becoming the
host of Venom, an alien symbiote whose species plans to invade Earth.

15
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
Following Venom's appearance in Spider-Man 3 (2007), Sony Pictures attempted to develop a spin-off film based on the
Venom character, which was stalled due to issues with the company's ongoing Spider-Man franchise.

16
01:04:00,000 --> 01:04:06,000
In March 2016, work began on a new version that would start a new shared universe featuring
the non-Spider-Man Marvel characters that the studio possessed film rights to.

17
01:08:00,000 --> 01:08:06,000
Sony also originally intended for the Venom film to share the world of the Marvel Cinematic Universe
film Spider-Man: Homecoming (2017), but ultimately distanced the film from Spider-Man.

18
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
Sony's Columbia Pictures produced the film in
association with Marvel Entertainment.

19
01:16:00,000 --> 01:16:06,000
In March 2017, Rosenberg and Pinkner were set to write, with Fleischer and Hardy
added in May; Marcel subsequently joined to rewrite the script.

20
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
Filming took place from October 2017 to January 2018 in
Atlanta, New York City, and San Francisco.

21
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:06,000
The film was primarily inspired by the comic book miniseries Venom: Lethal
Protector (1993) and the story arc "Planet of the Symbiotes" (1995).

22
01:28:00,000 --> 01:28:06,000
Ludwig Göransson was hired to compose the film's score, marking
his second Marvel film after Black Panther (2018).

23
01:32:00,000 --> 01:32:06,000
Venom premiered at the Regency Village Theater on October 1, 2018,
and was released in the United States on October 5.

24
01:36:00,000 --> 01:36:06,000
Despite generally negative reviews from critics, Hardy's performance and his character's relationship with Venom were praised, and the film became the
seventh-highest-grossing film of 2018, earning $856.1 million worldwide and setting several box office records for an October release.

25
01:40:00,000 --> 01:40:06,000
Two sequels have been released: Venom: Let There Be Carnage
(2021) and Venom: The Last Dance (2024).

26
01:44:00,000 --> 01:44:06,000
The film explores themes of spacecraft, san francisco,
california, superhero, anti hero, alien life-form.

27
01:48:00,000 --> 01:48:06,000
The tone is dark and thought_provoking.
